            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "JusJudy"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I had a big, bag of frozen broccoli around, because I'm trying to lose some weight and eat healthier. I dreaded, thinking about cooking it. I saw this recipe and thought it looked good! I made this as a side dish. It's awesome! I could have eaten a big, gigantic, bowl of this broccoli all by it's self! I added garlic like some suggested and man, is this good! That little bit of caramelization, the broccoli gets does the trick. I was never excited about frozen veggies before, but I could eat this every day.",
            "datePublished": "2012-01-24T16:42:03.547Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "clemsn"
            },
            "reviewBody": "How can broccoli be this good? I steamed fresh broccoli for maybe 2 or 2.5 minutes in a Corning ware bowl with a little water in the microwave. Then cooked as directed. My picky son asked for more!!! The combination of a little crispy and the heat of the red pepper flakes was a huge win! Thank you so much for a simple basic delicious way to eat broccoli!!!",
            "datePublished": "2020-10-25T23:24:47.317Z"
